{"kind":"report","text":"Technical reconciliation only; no Source approval or implementation/deployment authority.\n\nThe proposed three additive CLOSED blob4 place literals rpc:found, rpc:acts and rpc:preparations are a small sound reconciliation of Draft6 with current Source. I do not recommend overloading blob9 or classifying these public calls as dispatch: their actual public answer still belongs in blob9, independently of the native turn end in blob5. Nine blobs, six doubles, turn multiplicity and other meanings remain unchanged. Amend the place allowlist, examples, tests and section4.7 together before first-head review; this is an unshipped metrics-v1 clarification, not evidence of a deployed schema.\n\nCurrent Source supports the distinction: worker.ts api() is shared by route() and ScopeService; route assigns its HTTP context at the server-owned entry; ScopeService has no HTTP request and uses api(binding) directly. object.ts found/submit/prepare delegate to core public methods; core has early public answers before Turns.run. Hosted MCP also calls a ScopeApi transport. A hosted MCP HTTP request does not thereby become a /v1/scopes acts/found/preparations route: its underlying ScopeApi turn is rpc:* for this particular cross-count.\n\nUse server-owned ingress context beside args/answers only, with direct public API/object calls defaulting to rpc:*. Only the actual native HTTP entry wrapper can select the three existing HTTP places. Neither inbound trace headers, request IDs, Beside, signed intent fields nor an arbitrary caller-supplied place establish that classification or authority. Keep the public ScopeApi contract/answer bytes and retained entries, outbox and native delivery envelopes unchanged. Correlation IDs remain bounded untrusted operational values; create operational context for direct calls without inventing an HTTP route row. Keep per-invocation context distinct across concurrent calls.\n\nSet the entered-turn execution mark at the actual Turns.run boundary, not when the wrapper is called, the object is reached, an answer is accepted/refused or an HTTP status is selected. Propagate a mark beside the public answer only for that invocation. Confirmed early answers are pre-turn. A failed/missing internal operational reply must not be asserted as a confirmed pre-turn execution; retain an unknown/incomplete coverage signal under the existing loss mechanism when exact reconciliation cannot be established.\n\nSection4.7 should compare weighted route multiplicities with blob9=turn at found/acts/preparations against ONLY turn rows at those same HTTP places, preserving operation-specific comparison where resolution permits. Exclude rpc:* as well as alarm/dispatch from that HTTP pairing; do not manufacture route rows for RPC. Still count every RPC/internal native turn, and keep RPC busy/end/error signals visible in the appropriate all-turn views. Preserve the existing sampling, window-boundary and undetectable paired-loss limitations: this separation removes RPC masking, not all possible masking. A mixed/coarsened place that could include HTTP and RPC cannot be silently included in either count or discarded as proof of complete coverage. If it prevents the required discrimination, coverage is unknown/incomplete; preserve any observed busy failure independently.\n\nFocused acceptance cases for the Source owner: one HTTP route marked turn with its HTTP turn row missing plus an extra rpc:acts turn still yields an unsampled HTTP shortfall; HTTP and RPC calls have distinct places but the same actual accepted/refused/etc public-answer semantics; pre-turn failures create no entered-turn claim; a concurrent RPC call cannot borrow the HTTP context/mark; internal boolean-answer turns remain dispatch with blob9=none; mixed-place or missing-mark cases cannot report exact complete coverage. This request did not ask me to execute these tests or a gate.\n\nBasis: approved observability-design Draft6 tuple/turn instrumentation/section4.7 and read-only inspection of current worker.ts api/route/ScopeService, object.ts public methods, core.ts found/submit/prepare, turn.ts Turns.run and hosted.ts ScopeApi submission. No code changes, tests, provider calls or deployment.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5ea686895336e86cdc12ad873fd1148913afcd81","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a39306bac2a545d9d79c4b7a8017f9a6d2ccc48b"}}